  "name": "Courenta and balet (Occitan valleys of Piedmont dance music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The dance music of the Occitan-speaking valleys of south-western Piedmont, such as the Varaita, Maira and Vermenagna valleys in the province of Cuneo, built around the courenta, the balet and other dances played for village feasts on diatonic accordion, fiddle and hurdy-gurdy (ghironda), with songs in Occitan. A folk revival led by groups such as Lou Dalfin brought the ghironda back and carried the repertoire to festivals and records. The accordion card stands in for the valley diatonic button accordion.",
